// Floor 7 · «Casi perdido» · the cover's tones and glitter, traced from the photo (web/shots/covers/7-casi-perdido.jpg). Generated once, not by hand: the photo is a black paper in a plastic
// sleeve, so it was first unwarped to a square (the paper's four corners, a homography). The paper's own tone was estimated outside the figure only and taken out (so the face's dark greys stay),
// the luminance was lightly blurred and cut at five levels (marching squares), and every contour simplified (about a pixel). The gold glitter (saturated amber) and the silver glitter (warm pale grains,
// segmented by hue, saturation and brightness: the white paint is brighter and neutral) were taken apart from the white paint and out of the tones, and each got its own contours: its outline and its
// brighter facets. Each group is a list of closed loops, nested ones are holes (even-odd), in rectified cover pixels (the paper is 1100 square), as half-pixel integers: "n x0 y0 dx dy dx dy …", every number
// a variable-length code of 5 bits per character (the characters A-Z a-z 0-9 + - : 0-31 end a number, 32-63 continue it), deltas zig-zagged. Decoded by cpDecode() (decodeTones, 49-r3d-room-0-tones.js):
